 "poem": "FROM HER ROBING-SHIP - REV. JONAS de\nHAMILTON, HIS ISLANDS AND cit\nOft in my heart I see the glory\nOf England's long and holy war, namely,\nThe latest period of Restoration;\nIf I was one like her, as you contemplate\nThis great magnitude, I should be undone,\nAlthough on such an occasion great\nI would have been proud to walk away\nWith a manly face and brave, articulate\nVoice; but now, for my part, if she again\nFor ten or twenty years had been reigning",
